1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,210
Humiliation.
羞辱。

2
00:00:01,210 --> 00:00:03,990
Many of us have experienced it, right?
我们很多人都经历过，对吧？

3
00:00:03,990 --> 00:00:09,570
That horrific feeling of just wanting the ground to open up and swallow us.
那种恨不得找个地缝钻进去的糟糕感觉。

4
00:00:09,570 --> 00:00:15,300
It’s an awful sensation when someone decides to belittle us and make us feel small.
当有人刻意贬低我们、让我们自惭形秽时，那种滋味简直太难受了。

5
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:20,810
But what is humiliation, and how can we move on from it?
但究竟什么是羞辱？我们又该如何从这种情绪中走出来呢？

6
00:00:20,810 --> 00:00:25,220
Humiliation is quite often compared to the feeling of shame.
羞辱常常被拿来和羞耻感作比较。

7
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:33,200
However, the fundamental difference is that we feel shame is deserved, while humiliation is not.
但两者最根本的区别在于，我们会觉得羞耻是自己应得的，而羞辱并非如此。

8
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:36,900
It has more in common with bullying and harassment.
羞辱与霸凌和骚扰的共性更多。

9
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:50,320
Neel Burton M.D says that humiliation results from undermining claims that you have made, such as “I’m good at my job”, and challenges your authority to make such claims in future.
医学博士尼尔·伯顿表示，羞辱源于他人对你所宣称的自我价值的否定，比如你说“我工作很出色”，并会让你在未来都不敢再这样肯定自己。

10
00:00:50,320 --> 00:01:04,260
Imagine your colleague shocks you by unfairly calling you out on your work during a meeting with your boss. Or your friend may demean you by questioning your expertise in a hobby or interest in front of your other friends.
试想一下，在和老板开会时，你的同事毫无道理地指责你的工作；或者你的朋友在其他同伴面前，质疑你对某个爱好的专业度，以此贬低你。

11
00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:10,890
The presence of others is the key factor in humiliation – a public dressing-down.
羞辱的关键要素在于有他人在场——也就是公开斥责。

12
00:01:10,890 --> 00:01:15,210
It also has so many forms and uses in society.
在社会中，羞辱有着多种形式和用途。

13
00:01:15,210 --> 00:01:22,310
Public humiliation is often said to act as a crime deterrent, while it also has a place in comedy.
人们常说公开羞辱能起到震慑犯罪的作用，同时它在喜剧领域也占有一席之地。

14
00:01:22,310 --> 00:01:30,220
You may enjoy watching a celebrity being roasted: a humiliation designed to highlight faults for comedic effect.
你可能会喜欢看名人被调侃的场面：这种刻意为之的羞辱，是为了放大对方的缺点来制造喜剧效果。

15
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:33,400
So, how can you deal with it?
那么，该如何应对羞辱呢？

16
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:39,160
According to psychologist Robert J. Sternberg, there are a few steps you can take.
心理学家罗伯特·J·斯滕伯格指出，我们可以采取几个步骤。

17
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:50,060
First, you must accept the humiliation and realise you're not the only one who has felt like this – talk to others who have experienced it and move on.
首先，你必须接受自己被羞辱的事实，并意识到并非只有你有过这种感受——和其他有过类似经历的人聊一聊，然后放下过去继续前行。

18
00:01:50,060 --> 00:01:58,020
Also, don’t immediately try and strike back for ‘round 2’ – often humiliation isn’t personal.
此外，不要立刻想着反击再争高下——很多时候，羞辱并非针对你个人。

19
00:01:58,020 --> 00:02:02,580
Lastly, resilience seems to be crucial.
最后，韧性是至关重要的一点。

20
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:07,470
Some people say: “What doesn’t kill you only makes you stronger”.
有人说：“凡是杀不死你的，都会让你更强大。”

21
00:02:07,470 --> 00:02:11,960
While humiliation probably won't kill you, it can hurt.
虽然羞辱不至于置人于死地，但它确实会带来伤害。

22
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:19,760
Why not use the degradation as motivation to become a better worker or learn more about that hobby or interest?
何不把这种贬低当作动力，督促自己成为更优秀的职场人，或是更深入地钻研自己的爱好？

23
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:25,720
It could be an opportunity to start investing more in doing something you love.
这或许是一个契机，让你开始更多地投入到自己热爱的事情中去。

24
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:29,700
That way it may have an unexpected benefit.
这样一来，羞辱说不定还能带来意想不到的益处。
